Subject: [PATCH] monitor: keep retrying a refused DPMS commit

Against Hyprland v0.57.0 (src/output/Monitor.cpp).

commitDPMSState() retries a refused commit once, two frames later, and then
gives up. Hyprland already reports the new DPMS state, but the output stays
on. Aquamarine refuses an output commit while a page flip is busy: for
example CDRMOutput::commit() returns false while an asynchronous commit is
queued or in flight and can't be cancelled. A client that keeps rendering
when DPMS goes off keeps a flip pending most of the time, so both tries can
fail. Seen on a phone (gs-decon, 120 Hz) when an app kept animating as the
screen went off.

Keep retrying every two frames for up to a second, and damage the monitor
when a retried DPMS-on commit succeeds, as the first try does.

diff --git i/src/output/Monitor.cpp w/src/output/Monitor.cpp
--- i/src/output/Monitor.cpp
+++ w/src/output/Monitor.cpp
@@ -2253,12 +2253,14 @@
     if (!m_state.commit()) {
         LOG(Log::ERR, "Couldn't commit output {} for DPMS = {}, will retry.", m_name, state);
 
-        // retry in 2 frames. This could happen when the DRM backend rejects our commit
-        // because disable + enable were sent almost instantly
+        // retry every 2 frames. This could happen when the DRM backend rejects our commit
+        // because disable + enable were sent almost instantly, or because a page flip
+        // is still in flight while clients keep the output busy. Give up after a second.
 
-        m_dpmsRetryTimer = makeShared<CEventLoopTimer>(
-            std::chrono::milliseconds(2000 / sc<int>(m_refreshRate)),
-            [this, self = m_self](SP<CEventLoopTimer> s, void* d) {
+        const auto RETRY_MS = std::chrono::milliseconds(std::max(1, 2000 / sc<int>(m_refreshRate)));
+        m_dpmsRetryTimer    = makeShared<CEventLoopTimer>(
+            RETRY_MS,
+            [this, self = m_self, RETRY_MS, attempts = 0](SP<CEventLoopTimer> s, void* d) mutable {
                 if (!self)
                     return;
 
@@ -2266,11 +2268,17 @@
                 m_output->state->setEnabled(m_dpmsStatus);
 
                 if (!m_state.commit()) {
+                    if (++attempts * RETRY_MS < std::chrono::seconds(1)) {
+                        s->updateTimeout(RETRY_MS);
+                        return;
+                    }
                     LOG(Log::ERR, "Couldn't retry committing output {} for DPMS = {}", m_name, m_dpmsStatus);
                     return;
                 }
 
                 m_dpmsRetryTimer.reset();
+                if (m_dpmsStatus)
+                    g_pHyprRenderer->damageMonitor(m_self.lock());
             },
             nullptr);
         g_pEventLoopManager->addTimer(m_dpmsRetryTimer);
